{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BQEQHyApoxKhzVyeBApcbe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# M001 Layer Selection Fix Report\n2\t\n3\t**Date**: 2026-05-16  \n4\t**Status**: COMPLETE  \n5\t**Runtime**: 1301s (CPU-only)\n6\t\n7\t## Background\n8\t\n9\tThe original layer sweep (exp_001a, exp_001b) used `crossing_rate × lead_mean` as the layer selection metric. This metric is flawed: it rewards noisy early layers that exhibit random high crossing rates without genuine classification ability.\n10\t\n11\t## Fix Applied\n12\t\n13\tTwo alternative ranking schemes were evaluated:\n14\t- **Scheme A**: Pure `balanced_accuracy` (sklearn balanced_accuracy_score)\n15\t- **Scheme B**: `balanced_accuracy × crossing_rate` (joint optimization)\n16\t\n17\tScheme B was selected as primary because it balances classification quality with temporal detection capability.\n18\t\n19\t## Task 1: Layer Re-ranking\n20\t\n21\t### R1-32B (DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B)\n22\t\n23\t| Metric | Old (layer 2) | Corrected (layer 10) |\n24\t|--------|--------------|---------------------|\n25\t| Balanced Acc | 0.63 (est.) | 0.718 |\n26\t| Crossing Rate | 0.60 | 0.60 |\n27\t| Score (B) | - | 0.431 (rank 1) |\n28\t| Depth Ratio | 3.1% | 15.6% |\n29\t\n30\tScheme A best: layer 63 (bal_acc=0.755, but crossing_rate=0.25 only).\n31\t\n32\t### QwQ-32B\n33\t\n34\t| Metric | Old (layer 1) | Corrected (layer 2) |\n35\t|--------|--------------|---------------------|\n36\t| Balanced Acc | 0.71 (est.) | 0.730 |\n37\t| Crossing Rate | 0.47 | 0.47 |\n38\t| Score (B) | - | 0.346 (rank 1) |\n39\t| Depth Ratio | 1.6% | 3.1% |\n40\t\n41\tMinimal correction (1 layer shift). Layer 2 validated by balanced_accuracy.\n42\t\n43\t## Task 2: GRU Retraining (3 seeds)\n44\t\n45\t### R1-32B (layer 10, h=256, dropout=0.3)\n46\t\n47\t| Config | bal_acc | crossing | lead | pre-CP FPR |\n48\t|--------|---------|----------|------|------------|\n49\t| Single (mean) | 0.675 | 0.30 | 9.1 | 0.135 |\n50\t| Multi 9-layer (mean) | 0.655 | 0.23 | 8.8 | 0.114 |\n51\t\n52\tSingle-layer GRU outperforms multi-layer for R1-32B.\n53\t\n54\t### QwQ-32B (layer 2, h=256, dropout=0.3)\n55\t\n56\t| Config | bal_acc | crossing | lead | pre-CP FPR |\n57\t|--------|---------|----------|------|------------|\n58\t| Single (mean) | 0.694 | 0.75 | 19.3 | 0.303 |\n59\t| Multi 7-layer (mean) | 0.724 | 0.84 | 15.9 | 0.289 |\n60\t\n61\tMulti-layer GRU outperforms single-layer for QwQ-32B. Very high crossing rates (75-84%) with substantial lead times (16-19 steps).\n62\t\n63\t## Task 3: Temporal LR\n64\t\n65\t### R1-32B (layer 10)\n66\t\n67\t| Window | bal_acc | crossing | lead | pre-CP FPR |\n68\t|--------|---------|----------|------|------------|\n69\t| 5 | 0.731 | 0.55 | 11.8 | 0.239 |\n70\t| **10** | **0.737** | **0.50** | **9.0** | **0.189** |\n71\t| 15 | 0.721 | 0.60 | 7.5 | 0.209 |\n72\t\n73\tBest: window=10 (bal_acc=0.737).\n74\t\n75\t### QwQ-32B (layer 2)\n76\t\n77\t| Window | bal_acc | crossing | lead | pre-CP FPR |\n78\t|--------|---------|----------|------|------------|\n79\t| **5** | **0.761** | **0.42** | **23.5** | **0.180** |\n80\t| 10 | 0.747 | 0.42 | 20.8 | 0.171 |\n81\t| 15 | 0.741 | 0.47 | 17.6 | 0.161 |\n82\t\n83\tBest: window=5 (bal_acc=0.761, lead=23.5 steps).\n84\t\n85\t## Task 4: Paired Bootstrap (HS vs Text, R1-32B)\n86\t\n87\t| Probe | pre-CP FPR (mean +/- std) |\n88\t|-------|--------------------------|\n89\t| HS (layer 10, LR w=10) | 0.260 +/- 0.298 |\n90\t| Text (MiniLM-L6-v2, w=10) | 0.246 +/- 0.260 |\n91\t\n92\t- **Observed difference**: 0.014 (HS slightly worse)\n93\t- **p-value**: 0.999\n94\t- **95% CI**: [-0.103, 0.127]\n95\t- **Conclusion**: No significant difference. HS probe does NOT outperform text baseline on corrected layer for R1-32B.\n96\t\n97\t## Critical Implications\n98\t\n99\t1. **R1-32B HS advantage evaporates on corrected layer**: The previously reported HS superiority (p=0.848 on old layer 2) was likely an artifact of the flawed layer selection. On the correct layer (10), HS and text probes are statistically indistinguishable.\n100\t\n101\t2. **QwQ-32B remains robust**: Layer correction was minimal (1→2), and QwQ-32B still shows strong temporal detection (lead=23.5, crossing=42-84%).\n102\t\n103\t3. **Paper framing impact**: The claim that hidden-state monitoring provides unique value over text-based approaches needs re-evaluation for R1-32B. QwQ-32B results may still support the claim, but a single-model finding is weaker.\n104\t\n105\t## Output Files\n106\t\n107\tAll outputs at: `autodl-rtx6000:/root/autodl-tmp/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/m001_layer_fix/`\n108\t\n109\t- `layer_ranking_r1_32b.json` - Full 64-layer ranking both schemes\n110\t- `layer_ranking_qwq_32b.json` - Full 64-layer ranking both schemes\n111\t- `gru_corrected_r1_32b.json` - GRU results (3 seeds, single + multi)\n112\t- `gru_corrected_qwq_32b.json` - GRU results (3 seeds, single + multi)\n113\t- `temporal_lr_r1_32b.json` - Temporal LR (windows 5, 10, 15)\n114\t- `temporal_lr_qwq_32b.json` - Temporal LR (windows 5, 10, 15)\n115\t- `bootstrap_hs_vs_text_r1_32b.json` - Paired bootstrap (1000 resamples)\n116\t- `run.log` - Full execution log\n117\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e51f3ca8-7ac5-4490-8b2a-be7d501298c2","uuid":"76b79553-7129-4dea-b05a-09aa5847e9c6","timestamp":"2026-05-23T11:26:28.420Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/exp_001a_r1_32b/report/report_m001_layer_fix.md","content":"# M001 Layer Selection Fix Report\n\n**Date**: 2026-05-16  \n**Status**: COMPLETE  \n**Runtime**: 1301s (CPU-only)\n\n## Background\n\nThe original layer sweep (exp_001a, exp_001b) used `crossing_rate × lead_mean` as the layer selection metric. This metric is flawed: it rewards noisy early layers that exhibit random high crossing rates without genuine classification ability.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\nTwo alternative ranking schemes were evaluated:\n- **Scheme A**: Pure `balanced_accuracy` (sklearn balanced_accuracy_score)\n- **Scheme B**: `balanced_accuracy × crossing_rate` (joint optimization)\n\nScheme B was selected as primary because it balances classification quality with temporal detection capability.\n\n## Task 1: Layer Re-ranking\n\n### R1-32B (DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B)\n\n| Metric | Old (layer 2) | Corrected (layer 10) |\n|--------|--------------|---------------------|\n| Balanced Acc | 0.63 (est.) | 0.718 |\n| Crossing Rate | 0.60 | 0.60 |\n| Score (B) | - | 0.431 (rank 1) |\n| Depth Ratio | 3.1% | 15.6% |\n\nScheme A best: layer 63 (bal_acc=0.755, but crossing_rate=0.25 only).\n\n### QwQ-32B\n\n| Metric | Old (layer 1) | Corrected (layer 2) |\n|--------|--------------|---------------------|\n| Balanced Acc | 0.71 (est.) | 0.730 |\n| Crossing Rate | 0.47 | 0.47 |\n| Score (B) | - | 0.346 (rank 1) |\n| Depth Ratio | 1.6% | 3.1% |\n\nMinimal correction (1 layer shift). Layer 2 validated by balanced_accuracy.\n\n## Task 2: GRU Retraining (3 seeds)\n\n### R1-32B (layer 10, h=256, dropout=0.3)\n\n| Config | bal_acc | crossing | lead | pre-CP FPR |\n|--------|---------|----------|------|------------|\n| Single (mean) | 0.675 | 0.30 | 9.1 | 0.135 |\n| Multi 9-layer (mean) | 0.655 | 0.23 | 8.8 | 0.114 |\n\nSingle-layer GRU outperforms multi-layer for R1-32B.\n\n### QwQ-32B (layer 2, h=256, dropout=0.3)\n\n| Config | bal_acc | crossing | lead | pre-CP FPR |\n|--------|---------|----------|------|------------|\n| Single (mean) | 0.694 | 0.75 | 19.3 | 0.303 |\n| Multi 7-layer (mean) | 0.724 | 0.84 | 15.9 | 0.289 |\n\nMulti-layer GRU outperforms single-layer for QwQ-32B. Very high crossing rates (75-84%) with substantial lead times (16-19 steps).\n\n## Task 3: Temporal LR\n\n### R1-32B (layer 10)\n\n| Window | bal_acc | crossing | lead | pre-CP FPR |\n|--------|---------|----------|------|------------|\n| 5 | 0.731 | 0.55 | 11.8 | 0.239 |\n| **10** | **0.737** | **0.50** | **9.0** | **0.189** |\n| 15 | 0.721 | 0.60 | 7.5 | 0.209 |\n\nBest: window=10 (bal_acc=0.737).\n\n### QwQ-32B (layer 2)\n\n| Window | bal_acc | crossing | lead | pre-CP FPR |\n|--------|---------|----------|------|------------|\n| **5** | **0.761** | **0.42** | **23.5** | **0.180** |\n| 10 | 0.747 | 0.42 | 20.8 | 0.171 |\n| 15 | 0.741 | 0.47 | 17.6 | 0.161 |\n\nBest: window=5 (bal_acc=0.761, lead=23.5 steps).\n\n## Task 4: Paired Bootstrap (HS vs Text, R1-32B)\n\n| Probe | pre-CP FPR (mean +/- std) |\n|-------|--------------------------|\n| HS (layer 10, LR w=10) | 0.260 +/- 0.298 |\n| Text (MiniLM-L6-v2, w=10) | 0.246 +/- 0.260 |\n\n- **Observed difference**: 0.014 (HS slightly worse)\n- **p-value**: 0.999\n- **95% CI**: [-0.103, 0.127]\n- **Conclusion**: No significant difference. HS probe does NOT outperform text baseline on corrected layer for R1-32B.\n\n## Critical Implications\n\n1. **R1-32B HS advantage evaporates on corrected layer**: The previously reported HS superiority (p=0.848 on old layer 2) was likely an artifact of the flawed layer selection. On the correct layer (10), HS and text probes are statistically indistinguishable.\n\n2. **QwQ-32B remains robust**: Layer correction was minimal (1→2), and QwQ-32B still shows strong temporal detection (lead=23.5, crossing=42-84%).\n\n3. **Paper framing impact**: The claim that hidden-state monitoring provides unique value over text-based approaches needs re-evaluation for R1-32B. QwQ-32B results may still support the claim, but a single-model finding is weaker.\n\n## Output Files\n\nAll outputs at: `autodl-rtx6000:/root/autodl-tmp/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/m001_layer_fix/`\n\n- `layer_ranking_r1_32b.json` - Full 64-layer ranking both schemes\n- `layer_ranking_qwq_32b.json` - Full 64-layer ranking both schemes\n- `gru_corrected_r1_32b.json` - GRU results (3 seeds, single + multi)\n- `gru_corrected_qwq_32b.json` - GRU results (3 seeds, single + multi)\n- `temporal_lr_r1_32b.json` - Temporal LR (windows 5, 10, 15)\n- `temporal_lr_qwq_32b.json` - Temporal LR (windows 5, 10, 15)\n- `bootstrap_hs_vs_text_r1_32b.json` - Paired bootstrap (1000 resamples)\n- `run.log` - Full execution log\n","numLines":117,"startLine":1,"totalLines":117}}}
