/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1027-QwQ-32B & L63 & L51 & L39 & L44 & L44 & 24 layers & L50 \\\\\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:1028:R1-32B & L53 & L45 & L40 & L63 & L39 & 24 layers & L47 \\\\\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1029-\\bottomrule\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1030-\\end{tabular}}\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1031-\\end{table}\n--\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1039-\\subsection{Nested Cross-Validation}\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1040-\\label{app:nested_cv}\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1041-\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:1042:The holdout estimates in \\cref{tab:hs_vs_text} select layer and window on the validation fold, then evaluate on a fixed test set. To rule out hyperparameter overfitting, we run nested 5-fold cross-validation on both 7--8B models: the outer fold holds out test data; the inner loop selects (layer, $W$) on the remaining four folds. \\cref{tab:nested_cv} reports per-fold precision differences.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1043-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1044-\\begin{table}[htbp]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1045-\\centering\n--\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1061-\\end{flushleft}\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1062-\\end{table}\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1063-\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:1064:[Omitted long matching line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1065-\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1066-\\paragraph{Formal test.} A one-sided Wilcoxon signed-rank test on the 5-fold $\\Delta$precision (HS$-$text) rejects $H_0{:}\\;\\Delta{=}0$ for both models ($W{=}15$, $p{=}0.031$; the minimum achievable $p$-value at $n{=}5$). Layer selection entropy across folds is $H{=}1.37$ bits for R1-8B (normalized 0.59; dominated by L12 in 3/5 folds) and $H{=}1.92$ bits for OT-7B (normalized 0.83; L21--L27), indicating moderately stable layer selection for R1-8B and higher variability for OT-7B.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1067-\n--\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1115-\\begin{table}[htbp]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1116-\\centering\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1117-\\small\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:1118:\\caption{R1-8B FPR per-seed comparison (L14, $W{=}15$; main text \\cref{tab:hs_vs_text} reports $W{=}3$ after 5-seed validation). Direction is consistent (5/5 HS $\\leq$ Text); 2/5 reach $p{<}0.05$ uncorrected, 1/5 after Bonferroni correction (5 seeds, $\\alpha{=}0.01$).}\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1119-\\label{tab:r18b_fpr_seeds}\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/docs/paper/sections/appendix.tex-1120-\\resizebox{\\columnwidth}{!}{%\n/home/ubuntu/.