{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014hbFqcUzJPE62p54S2w9VR","type":"tool_result","content":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T212242/median/experiment_data.json:    \"description\": \"10,000 bootstrap resamples for all key comparisons. AUROC, PR curves, detection delay CDF. Validates statistical rigor of all claims.\\n\",\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T212242/median/experiment_data.json:    \"analysis\": \"Statistical rigor is the paper's strongest suit (soundness 3.5-4.0). 12/12 HB is impressive. But R3 argues \\\"statistical significance ≠ practical significance\\\" and points to the high FPR as evidence that the statistically significant precision advantage doesn't translate to deployable monitoring.\\n\\n\\n12/12 HB is the paper's statistical anchor. But median-tier reviewers probe deeper: R3 notes that QwQ FPR (p=0.006) and R1-32B FPR (p=0.010) are the weakest links — \\\"marginal at corrected layers, wouldn't survive a stricter family-wise correction.\\\" The 10,000 resamples improve precision over 1,000 but the marginal p-values barely change. AUROC analysis reveals that AUROC-optimal layers differ from threshold-dependent layers (AUROC prefers mid-depth ~50%), which R2 flags as \\\"another researcher degree of freedom.\\\" The statistical story is sound (rating 3.5-4.0 on soundness) but doesn't compensate for limited novelty.\\n\"\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T212242/worst/experiment_data.json:    \"description\": \"10000 bootstrap resamples on all key metrics across 4 models. Holm-Bonferroni correction. AUROC, precision-recall curves, detection delay CDF.\\n\",\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T212242/worst/experiment_data.json:    \"analysis\": \"FPR analysis is the worst-tier's core evidence for the \\\"not practically useful\\\" dismissal. No model meets all three deployment criteria simultaneously. The best model (R1-8B) achieves >70% precision only at W≥15 where coverage drops to 49%. The paper's deployment framing is untenable. Reframing guidance: \\\"Position as diagnostic/research tool, explicitly disclaim deployment readiness. Lead with 'none of our 7 methods achieves deployment-ready performance' as a cautionary finding.\\\"\\n\\n\\nSafe FPR ranges from 11% (OT-7B HS static, best case) to 52% (GRU, worst case), with a median around 39%. This is the worst-tier dealbreaker. Reviewer calculation: \\\"At 39% safe FPR with K=5 consecutive crossings for trace-level detection, a 40-step safe trace has ~39% probability of triggering the detector. In a production system processing 1000 safe traces per day, that's ~390 false alarms daily. Each requires human review at ~5 minutes → 32.5 person-hours/day of false alarm triage. No deployment team would accept this.\\\" Even the best case (OT-7B HS 11.1% safe FPR) means 111 false alarms per 1000 safe traces. The worst-tier reviewer's verdict: \\\"A safety monitor that fires on 1 in 3 to 1 in 2 safe traces is not a monitor — it's a random noise generator. The paper should lead with this limitation, not bury it.\\\" QwQ-32B is particularly problematic: HS safe FPR (45-50%) is HIGHER than text safe FPR (33-43%), meaning HS monitoring generates MORE false alarms on safe traces for QwQ.\\n\"\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T212242/best/experiment_data.json:    \"description\": \"10,000 bootstrap resamples, Holm-Bonferroni step-down correction, 4 models × 3 metrics = 12 tests。报告 AUROC, PR curves, FPR。\\n\",\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T212242/best/experiment_data.json:      \"n_resamples\": 10000,\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260522T085530/worst/experiment_data.json:    \"description\": \"10000 bootstrap resamples on key metrics across 4 models. Holm-Bonferroni correction. AUROC, PR curves, detection delay CDF.\\n\",\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260522T085530/best/experiment_data.json:    \"description\": \"4模型×3指标=12项Holm-Bonferroni检验。10000 resamples。全部通过。\\n\",\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260522T085530/best/experiment_data.json:      \"resamples\": 10000,\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260522T085530/best/experiment_data.json:    \"analysis\": \"12/12 HB pass是论文统计backbone。 precision一致性惊人（+15-28pp across 4 models）。 FPR是最marginal的指标（rank 9-12），但全部通过。\\n\\n\\nCorrected layers解锁了全部12/12显著性（vs biased layers的5/12）。 核心原因：biased层（L2/L10）的HS信号弱，效应量小，n=20-47无法检出； corrected层（L14/L16/L60/L63）效应量大（precision +15-28pp）， 即使n=20也有足够power（MDE 9-11pp << 实际效应15-28pp）。 10000 resamples vs 1000无实质差异，但消除了p-value Monte Carlo noise。\\n\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JKUhSfYJcgTbWe9fLFD6bA","session_id":"e51f3ca8-7ac5-4490-8b2a-be7d501298c2","uuid":"9249edee-9a1b-4f13-98fc-acc33d4dfe3c","timestamp":"2026-05-23T11:37:06.068Z"}
